  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\left(1-x+x^2\\right)^n=a_0+a_1 x+\\ldots . .+a_{2 n} x^{2 n}$, then the value of $a_0+a_2+a_4+\\ldots \\ldots .+a_{2 n}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "DIgbb",
      "text": "$3^{\\mathrm{n}}+\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tWOoG",
      "text": "$3^{\\mathrm{n}}-\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "47ep7",
      "text": "$\\frac{3^{\\mathrm{n}}-1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GVnQG",
      "text": "$\\frac{3^{\\mathrm{n}}+1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: $x=1$\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\n1=a_0+a_1+a_2+a_3+\\ldots \\ldots \\ldots+a_{2 n} \\\\\nx=-1,3^{\\mathrm{n}}=a_0-a_1+a_2-a_3+\\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots+a_{2 n} \\\\\n1+3^{\\mathrm{n}}=2\\left[a_0+a_2+a_4+\\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots+a_{2 \\mathrm{n}}\\right] \\\\\n\\Rightarrow a_0+a_2+a_4+\\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots+a_{2 \\mathrm{n}}=\\frac{1+3^{\\mathrm{n}}}{2}\n\\end{gathered}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
